Description: Wild OS Files, the file manager
 Files is the Wild OS file manager, laid out like File Explorer on
 Windows 11: tabs in the title bar, a breadcrumb address bar, a command
 bar, and Home folders, drives and the Recycle Bin in the sidebar. File name
 extensions are hidden for known types. Folders are read and changed
 through KIO, so the Recycle Bin, network places and removable drives all work.
 .
 With Advanced protection, Files saves copies of photos, videos, audio,
 PDFs and Office documents without their location, device and author
 details, and opens unknown programs and attachments in a safe box sealed
 off from Home and the network.
